Z||000003||StuGood||05-10-2001||03:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Syncro's are probley off   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, I don't think reverse gear cares about the synchros, sorry.  <P>Next time you try it, hold both clutch and brake pedals down (car stationary), and shift into 2nd (or any gear besides reverse), <B>then</B> into reverse.  <P>Shifting into 2nd stops the trans. from spinning, so that you can get into reverse without clashing.  This has nothing to do with what you're wearing vs. interior color, BTW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If that doesn't work, clutch probably is not releasing fully.||||reg||5
